    },
    {
      "text": "All right $META Muse is cooking. \n\nI can hear all the $AMD, $INTC, and $ARM CPUs vrrrring in the background.\n\nAlong with the memory + components (NICs, SSDs, DRAM) needed for all the browsers/VMs\n\nWhen I ask it to do a bunch of long form tasks… \n\nIntel CEO also said recently that CPU demand is so strong they can only support 50% of what customers need, so there’s some signals there.\n\nI’m also curious how much $AMZN or $NBIS is involved with running Muse, or if Meta hosts everything inhouse.\n\nKinda an ADHD post but Meta beat my expectations with this release.\n\nWill keep trying it out",
